<title>BULGARIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>BULGARIA GOVERNMENT LIST (961104)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> *  4 Nov 96 - Results from the November 3 presidential	*</p>
<p> *		 election runoff showed opposition candidate   *</p>
<p> *		 Petar Stoyanov had won about 60 percent of the*</p>
<p> *		 vote against Ivan Marazov's 40 percent.	 *</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p>President (Elected 1 August 1990, re-elected</p>
<p>	19 January 1992 for a five-year term)......Zhelyu ZHELEV</p>
<p> Vice-President.......................................Vacant**</p>
<p>	    (**To remain vacant until elections in January 1997)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Prime Minister (Elected 25 Jan 95)...............Zhan VIDENOV</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (Formed 26 Jan 95, reshuffled 10 Jun 96)</p>
<p> Prime Minister...................................Zhan VIDENOV</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister.......................Doncho KONAKCHIEV</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Territorial Development &amp; Construction)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister...........................Roumen GECHEV</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Economic Development)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister......................Svetoslav SHIVAROV</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture...............................Krastio TRENDAFILOV</p>
<p> Culture..........................................Ivan MARAZOV</p>
<p> Defence........................................Dimitar PAVLOV</p>
<p> Economic Development...........................See Deputy PMs</p>
<p> Education, Science &amp; Technologies..............Ilcho DIMITROV</p>
<p> Energy........................................Roumen OVCHAROV</p>
<p> Environment..........................Georgi Dimitrov GEORGIEV</p>
<p> Finance........................................Dimitar KOSTOV</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs...............................Georgi PIRINSKI</p>
<p> Health..........................................Mimmi VITKOVA</p>
<p> Industry......................................Lyubomir DACHEV</p>
<p> Interior.......................................Nikolai DOBREV</p>
<p> Justice...................................Mladen CHERVENYAKOV</p>
<p> Social Care &amp; Labour..........................Mincho KORALSKI</p>
<p> Territorial Development &amp; Construction.........See Deputy PMs</p>
<p> Trade........................................Atanas PAPARIZOV</p>
<p> Transport.....................................Stamen STAMENOV</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Parliamentary Speaker........................Blagovest SENDOV</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor........................Lyubomir FILIPOV</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			 (End government list)</p>
